 "voice": [
  {
   "id": "vo01",
   "t": 0.1,
   "dur": 4.061,
   "file": "vo/01.wav",
   "text": "What's this cell carrying? Room for about a billion passengers."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo02",
   "t": 5.1,
   "dur": 8.88,
   "file": "vo/02.wav",
   "text": "It's stuffed with one protein, hemoglobin: about a quarter of a billion copies. Each one has four iron seats, and each seat holds one oxygen."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo03",
   "t": 14.7,
   "dur": 9.056,
   "file": "vo/03.wav",
   "text": "Watch one fill. The first oxygen struggles to get on, but each one makes the next one easier. Empty, it's dark red; full, it's bright red."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo04",
   "t": 24.7,
   "dur": 12.36,
   "file": "vo/04.wav",
   "text": "Veins often look blue, so it's easy to guess the blood inside is too. It never is. Blood heading home is darker red. Red light sinks in, the vein swallows it, so less red bounces back."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo05",
   "t": 39.9,
   "dur": 9.731,
   "file": "vo/05.wav",
   "text": "Your heart sends your blood back through your lungs about once a minute. There, the empty seats fill. In about a quarter of a second."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo06",
   "t": 53.5,
   "dur": 5.489,
   "file": "vo/06.wav",
   "text": "The blue is your skin's trick. The red is a passenger count: brighter means fuller seats."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo07",
   "t": 59.9,
   "dur": 4.684,
   "file": "vo/07.wav",
   "text": "Meanwhile, as you watched, your blood handed your body about a cup of oxygen."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo08",
   "t": 65.5,
   "dur": 4.733,
   "file": "vo/08.wav",
   "text": "Next: the signal in your nerves. In the fastest, it doesn't crawl; it jumps."
  }
 ]
}